<title>ESTONIA: SOCCER-FLORA BEATEN BY SWEDISH TEAM IN CYRPUS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-FLORA BEATEN BY SWEDISH TEAM IN CYRPUS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>FC Flora, one of Estonia's leading soccer clubs, was narrowly defeated in a penalty shoot out by Swedish club Hammarby on Thursday in Cyprus.</p>
<p>Flora said the game ran for normal time for a 0:0 draw but the game was won after Hammarby shot four penalities against Flora's three.</p>
<p>FC Flora next game will be on Saturday in the northern countries' soccer competition on the Mediterranean island.</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
